# Leaf spec: shaft machining kinematics and camera curves (producer)

Objective: closed-form machining kinematics and authored camera curves for the 43 s shaft story, sampled from one master playhead.

Context (read, do not modify): docs/jgun-manufacturing-inspection-plan.md sections 2 and 4 (owner storyline: shaper cuts, slow exit macro, recap, material cards, revised blank, hobbing, supports, finale); project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/camera/clearance-v4/README.md and report.json (CERTIFIED illustrative tool dimensions and paths; use these numbers exactly); src/scene/inspection/shaft/story.ts (shaftBeats authored table, 43 s) and shaft/script.ts (cards/stress timing; cool scan starts 32.8 s, so hob withdrawal must be complete by 32.0 s); src/scene/inspection/timeline.ts (closed-form allocation-free sampler style with caller-owned out objects); src/scene/inspection/story.ts (StoryRuntime interfaces). Shaft-local frame: +Y is the shaft axis in millimetres in CAD; the runtime GLB (public/models/manufacturing-core-full.glb, nodes legacyshaft/approvedshaft/housing/legacybearing/legacyring/approvedbearing/approvedring) is metres with shaft-local +Y exported to glTF -Z (one conversion only). Measured: 10 teeth, 36 deg pitch, tip r 6.0834, root r 4.2918, face y 3.1749..9.5249, legacy last tooth material y 9.875, legacy groove floor r 3.97 at y 10.41, groove wall y 10.94; approved ramp floor ends y 13.78 at filler OD 6.074; approved journal r 6.325 from y 14.18.
Rules: you are not alone in the codebase; never revert or stage others' work; no git operations; do not read TODO.md or queue docs (this spec is complete). Everything must be a pure function of time (no accumulators, no Math.random/Date/performance), allocation-free in per-frame paths, deterministic under any seek order. Do not register stories, mount components or edit shared scene files.

Files you own (create only): src/scene/inspection/shaft/kinematics.ts, kinematics.test.ts, src/scene/inspection/shaft/camera.ts, camera.test.ts, project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/gates/shaft-kinematics-camera.md. Read project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/camera/blockout.json and camera/tool-conventions.md for blockout shot positions (desktop and 390x844) as starting values; re-centre on the certified tool positions where needed.

Kinematics (sampleShaftKinematics(t, out)):
- Machining-time map m(t): continuous, monotonic, piecewise-smooth (C1) function of the master playhead. Shaping 2..15 s: normal speed 2..6, ease down into a slow interval covering the cutter exit (>= 1.2 s of stable-camera slow action within 6..11 including ~0.4 s of unmistakable clearance during the relieved return), ease back up, then a visibly time-compressed recap 11..15 that completes all remaining tooth spaces before 15 s. Hobbing 25..32: feed hob centre from -4.195 to 9.5249 mm, retract 2.5 mm radially and withdraw so the hob is clear and out of the runout view by 32.0 s.
- Shaper: cutter rotation phi_c(m), work rotation phi_w = -2 * phi_c (signed ratio work/cutter -2), stroke y(m) between the certified stroke centre limits (cutting toward +Y, relieved return backed off 2.0 mm), radial infeed reaching full depth during the first quarter orbit then holding. Per tooth-space depth depth_i(t) in [0,1] derived from engagement: a space gains depth only when it passes the cutter mesh point while the cutter is cutting; expose spaceDepth[10], engagedSpace, edgeY consistent with progression.ts semantics (Float32Array owned by the caller). All 10 spaces reach depth 1 by 15.0 s.
- Hob: rotation phi_h(m), work rotation phi_w = phi_h / 10 (single start, 10 teeth; sign documented), hobYc(m), hobA(m).
- Chip: one restrained chip at the shaper rake face only while stock is removed (closed-form position/curl/opacity from stroke phase; seeded deterministically); none during return.
- Display-rate guard: stroke and gash frequencies on screen must stay <= one quarter of 30 fps, or expose a 'softened' flag for the renderer to blur/fade repeated features; test it over the timeline.
